From fdc307a2e0740a9ff95b2dd9e1d8e2aacacdac28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:03:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] intel/ds: Initialize perfetto before registering render
 stages on Android

The Android port does not call util_perfetto_init() from
util_cpu_trace_init(), because eglGetDisplay() runs in zygote's GL
driver preload and the perfetto thread makes zygote hang before fork
("Perfetto: Modify to make perfetto and AGI run ok").

Mesa 26.0 no longer calls util_perfetto_init() in
intel_driver_ds_init_once() either, so IntelRenderpassDataSource was
registered on the fake tracing muxer and perfetto aborted
(FailUninitialized -> SIGILL) in iris_screen_create(), crashing
surfaceflinger in eglInitialize() and leaving the display blank.

Initialize perfetto right before registering the data source, as the
25.0.1 tree did. This runs at iris screen / anv device creation only.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1589
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
---
 src/intel/ds/intel_driver_ds.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/intel/ds/intel_driver_ds.cc b/src/intel/ds/intel_driver_ds.cc
index d0cbd2032ba5..be41c9eec597 100644
--- a/src/intel/ds/intel_driver_ds.cc
+++ b/src/intel/ds/intel_driver_ds.cc
@@ -673,6 +673,14 @@ static void
 intel_driver_ds_init_once(void)
 {
 #ifdef HAVE_PERFETTO
+#if DETECT_OS_ANDROID
+   /* util_cpu_trace_init() does not initialize perfetto on Android (see
+    * cpu_trace.h), so do it here: registering a data source before
+    * perfetto::Tracing::Initialize() is fatal. This runs at screen/device
+    * creation, not in the zygote GL driver preload.
+    */
+   util_perfetto_init();
+#endif
    perfetto::DataSourceDescriptor dsd;
 #if DETECT_OS_ANDROID
    // Android tooling expects this data source name
